        "caption": {
          "zh": "1874年 · 纽约大都会艺术博物馆",
          "en": "1874 · The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT I",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第一幕 · 一份委托",
          "en": "A commission"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "1873年，著名的歌剧男中音让-巴蒂斯特·福尔，请德加画一幅芭蕾舞者上课或考试的画。",
          "en": "In 1873, the famous opera baritone Jean-Baptiste Faure commissioned Degas to paint ballet dancers at a class or examination."
        }
      },
      {
        "image": "images/dance-class.jpg",
        "alt": {
          "zh": "德加《舞蹈课》1874，纽约大都会艺术博物馆",
          "en": "Edgar Degas, The Dance Class, 1874, The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York"
        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1874年 · 纽约大都会艺术博物馆",
          "en": "1874 · The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT II",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第二幕 · 想象的教室",
          "en": "An imagined classroom"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "19世纪70年代前半期，德加花了很多时间在巴黎歌剧院，观察教室、排练室和舞台上的课程和排练。但这间教室是他想象出来的：它所在的旧歌剧院，不久前刚被烧毁。",
          "en": "In the early 1870s, Degas spent a great deal of time at the Paris Opéra, watching classes and rehearsals. But this room is imagined: the old opera house it belonged to had recently burned down."
        }
      },
      {
        "image": "images/dance-class.jpg",
        "alt": {
          "zh": "德加《舞蹈课》1874，纽约大都会艺术博物馆",
          "en": "Edgar Degas, The Dance Class, 1874, The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York"
        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1874年 · 纽约大都会艺术博物馆",
          "en": "1874 · The Metropolitan Museum of Art, New York"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT III",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第三幕 · 两个版本",
          "en": "Two versions"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "1876年，福尔把这幅画借给了印象派画展。这一幅和奥赛博物馆的另一版本，是德加以舞蹈为主题最有雄心的两幅作品。今天，它在纽约大都会艺术博物馆的815展厅。",
          "en": "In 1876, Faure lent the painting to the Impressionist exhibition. This work and its variant in the Musée d'Orsay are Degas's most ambitious paintings of dance. Today it hangs in Gallery 815 of the Metropolitan Museum."
        }
      }
    ],
